      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Overtones create the unique spectral signature of a flute, transforming a simple fundamental frequency into a rich, musical tone rather than a hollow beep. While the fundamental pitch defines the note's height, the mixture of specific overtone harmonics gives the flute its distinctive brightness and character compared to other instruments like the clarinet. Without these overtones, a flute would effectively lose its identity and suffer from poor projection in an acoustic space.",
